Timestamps + per-stream handle deque could add multistreaming to the static dry-run-based allocator.
  If one CPU thread:
    cudaDeviceSynchronize
      Move per-stream handles to "globally available" handle stack that will be checked as a second-to-last resort before allocating a new handle.
      Delete all per-stream pools (rebuild lazily, as if from the beginning of the program).
    cudaStreamSynchronize or cudaEventSynchronize
      Move that stream's handles to "globally available" stack.
      Delete that stream's pool (rebuild lazily if the stream is used again).
